{"team":"LA","col":"#c9d5e0","identity":"balanced","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":61.7,"adot":8.6,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>No Fixed Address</h2><p>The backfield runs through one man \u2014 <strong>Kyren Williams</strong> absorbs <strong>68% of the carries</strong> (league ~59%), a true bell-cow share that makes his rushing volume among the safest floors in the sport when the script cooperates.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>They're a heavy under-center team (48% shotgun vs ~68%) \u2014 a pro-style, run-committed structure.</p><p>They run downhill \u2014 mostly inside the tackles (18% to the edge vs ~25%), a gap/power scheme that trades big plays for a steady, grinding floor.</p><p>This is an aggressive, pass-leaning attack: <strong>-0%</strong> pass rate over expected, top of the league's range, and no interest in sitting on a lead (44% pass when ahead).</p><p>The tight end is barely used in the passing game (9% of targets vs ~15%) \u2014 fade their TE's receiving props.</p><p>The WR2 is unusually involved here \u2014 <strong>19%</strong> of targets (league ~15%), meaning there's bankable volume beyond the top receiver.</p><p>By the numbers it's an efficient unit \u2014 a 49% success rate (above the 44% average).</p><p>They push it downfield \u2014 average depth of target <strong>8.6 yards</strong> with 23% of throws traveling 15+, a vertical passing game that trades completions for boom-or-bust yardage.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Their red-zone identity is <strong>pass-first</strong> (55% pass), which puts scoring equity on <strong>Puka Nacua</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 Soft on the Ground</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing WR1s</strong> \u2014 68 rec yds/game (vs ~58). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They surrender <strong>124 rushing</strong> and <strong>239 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p><strong>Soft against opposing tight ends</strong> \u2014 41 rec yds/game (vs ~35). A rec-yards target.</p><p><strong>Soft against backs out of the backfield</strong> \u2014 23 rec yds/game (vs ~18). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They leak <strong>WR1 receiving TDs</strong> (0.59/game vs ~0.38) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Matthew Stafford","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":6,"props":{"Comp":21.07,"Att":32.27,"Pass Yds":247.79,"Pass TD":1.83,"INT":0.55,"Rush Yds":4.1},"d":{"completions":21.07,"attempts":32.27,"pass_yards":247.79,"pass_td":1.83,"interceptions":0.55,"rush_att":2.08,"rush_yards":4.1}}],"RB":[{"name":"Kyren Williams","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":47,"props":{"Rush Att":13.76,"Rush Yds":63.49,"Tgt":4.22,"Rec":3.23,"Rec Yds":21.25},"d":{"rush_att":13.76,"rush_yards":63.49,"targets":4.22,"receptions":3.23,"rec_yards":21.25,"rec_td":0.17}},{"name":"Blake Corum","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":21,"props":{"Rush Att":8.39,"Rush Yds":38.85,"Tgt":2.56,"Rec":1.97,"Rec Yds":14.07},"d":{"rush_att":8.39,"rush_yards":38.85,"targets":2.56,"receptions":1.97,"rec_yards":14.07,"rec_td":0.05}},{"name":"Ronnie Rivers","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":9,"props":{"Rush Att":3.15,"Rush Yds":12.98,"Tgt":2.47,"Rec":1.75,"Rec Yds":12.24},"d":{"rush_att":3.15,"rush_yards":12.98,"targets":2.47,"receptions":1.75,"rec_yards":12.24,"rec_td":0.04}}],"WR":[{"name":"Puka Nacua","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":35,"props":{"Tgt":12.51,"Rec":8.87,"Rec Yds":119.42,"Rec TD":0.43},"d":{"targets":12.51,"receptions":8.87,"rec_yards":119.42,"rec_td":0.43}},{"name":"Davante Adams","slot":"WR2","starter":true,"td":33,"props":{"Tgt":8.26,"Rec":5.11,"Rec Yds":65.82,"Rec TD":0.4},"d":{"targets":8.26,"receptions":5.11,"rec_yards":65.82,"rec_td":0.4}}